rsz: after a journal restore, update parasitics and let STA re-time lazily

Per-pass cost experiment from the repair-knobs campaign
(ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md, third study). Not upstreamed; carried while
it is measured. Whether it changes any result is what the measurement
says: the final ODB hash decides.

Every time the setup sweep gives up on an endpoint it restores the ECO
journal, and MoveCommitter::restoreJournal ends with
Resizer::updateParasiticsAndTiming(): the undone nets get their
parasitics back and sta_->findRequireds() re-times the design. The
per-visit trace of the default (patches/0078, 0066) puts journal restore
at 14-36% of the setup phase (ibex floorplan: 25 s of 71 over 480
restores), and 0081 showed the design-area recount in the same path is
not where those seconds go; the STA update is what is left.

The next pass calls findRequireds after its own moves, and the next
endpoint reads its slack through STA's lazy incremental search, so the
explicit update here re-times the undone cone once on its own and then
again merged with the next change. This patch keeps the parasitics
update and drops the timing update from the restore.

Chesterton's Fence: the update was there so that no stale slack is read
after an undo; OpenSTA's incremental search is what guarantees that on
every query, and the measurement checks the ODB hash to be sure.
diff --git a/src/rsz/include/rsz/Resizer.hh b/src/rsz/include/rsz/Resizer.hh
index 86a6e4ff73..9decbf5873 100644
--- a/src/rsz/include/rsz/Resizer.hh
+++ b/src/rsz/include/rsz/Resizer.hh
@@ -928,6 +928,9 @@ class Resizer : public sta::dbStaState, public sta::dbNetworkObserver
   void journalMakeBuffer(sta::Instance* buffer);
   void initForJournalRestore();
   void updateParasiticsAndTiming();
+  // The parasitics half of the above, for a caller that lets STA re-time
+  // lazily at its next query.
+  void updateParasiticsOnly();
   void invalidateParasitics(sta::Net* net);
   void addAcceptedLegacyMoveCount(int count);
   void addRejectedLegacyMoveCount(int count);
diff --git a/src/rsz/src/MoveCommitter.cc b/src/rsz/src/MoveCommitter.cc
index fa93ecd3cf..b297145e1f 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/MoveCommitter.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/MoveCommitter.cc
@@ -583,7 +583,14 @@ void MoveCommitter::restoreJournal()
   }
 
   if (had_eco_changes) {
-    resizer_.updateParasiticsAndTiming();
+    // Study candidate (repair-yield): the undone nets get their parasitics
+    // back now, but the timing update is left to the next query. The
+    // caller's next pass calls findRequireds after its own moves anyway,
+    // and the sweep's next endpoint reads its slack through STA's lazy
+    // incremental search; the explicit findRequireds here re-timed the
+    // undone cone once on its own and once more merged with the next
+    // pass's cone. Journal restore is 14-36% of the setup phase.
+    resizer_.updateParasiticsOnly();
     resizer_.invalidateVertexOrdering();
   }
 
